{"id":"word:hebrew:H8628","type":"word","title":"תָּקַע","subtitle":"H8628 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"to clatter , i.e. slap (the hands together), clang (an instrument); by analogy, to drive (a nail or tent-pin, a dart, etc.); by implication, to become bondsman by handclasping)","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to תָּקַע (H8628) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: v.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 70 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"תָּקַע (tâqaʻ) means to clatter , i.e. slap (the hands together), clang (an instrument); by analogy, to drive (a nail or tent-pin, a dart, etc.); by implication, to become bondsman by handclasping) First listed occurrence: 1Chr 10 10."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"תָּקַע","transliteration":"tâqaʻ","pronunciation":"taw-kah'","strong":"H8628","lemmaId":"hebrew:H8628","partOfSpeech":"v","forms":["וַֽ/יִּתְקְעוּ֙","יִתְקְע֖וּ","וְ/תָקְע֖וּ","וַ/יִּתְקַ֤ע","וַ/יִּתְקַע֙"],"morphs":[["HVqv2mp",8],["HVqp3cp",7],["HC/Vqw3mp",6],["HC/Vqw3ms",6],["HC/Vqq2mp",5],["HVqp3ms",4],["HVqi3mp",4],["HVNi3ms",3],["HC/Vqq3cp",3],["HC/Vqrmsa",2]]},"definitions":{"short":"to clatter , i.e. slap (the hands together), clang (an instrument); by analogy, to drive (a nail or tent-pin, a dart, etc.); by implication, to become bondsman by handclasping)","usage":"blow (a trumpet), cast, clap, fasten, pitch (tent), smite, sound, strike, × suretiship, thrust.","full":"H8628. taqa תָּקַע verb thrust, clap, give a blow, blast (Late Hebrew id. ; Jewish-Aramaic תְּקַע strike, blow horn ; Ethiopic blow trumpet); — Qal Perfect 3masculine singular ׳ת Gen 31:25 +, 1 singular וְתָקַעְתִּ֫י Jer 7:18 , etc.; Imperfect 3masculine singular תִּקְעוּ Jeremiah 3:37 +, suffix וַיִּתְקָעֵהוּ Exod 10:19 , etc.; Imperative masculine plural תִּקְעוּ Hosea 5:8 +; Infinitive absolute תָּקוֺעַ Josh 6:9 , 13 ; construct לִתְקוֺעַ Judg 7:12 , ׳כִּת Isa 18:3 ; Participle active תִּקֵעַ Prov 17:18 +, ect.; passive feminine תְּקוּעָה Isa 22:25 ; &#8212; 1 thrust, drive , weapon (accusative) into ( ב ) a person Judg 3:21 ; 4:21 ; 2Sam 18:14 , peg into ( ב ) something Isa 22:23 , 25 (compare Judg 4:21 ); hence pitch a tent (accusative), i.e. drive its pegs: Gen 31:25 a Jer 6:3 ( + עַל against, in figure), accusative omitted Gen 31:25 b; thrust, drive, beat (strands of hair together) בַּיָּחֵד Judg 16:4 , insert a; so 16:13 (so ᵐ5 ; compare GFM Comm. and PAOS Oct, 1889, 176 ff. ); thrust, drive locusts seaward ( ה locative), Exod 10:19 (J); compare ׳ת בְּ 1Sam 31:10 of fastening bodies to wall, and similarly 1Chr 10:10 (but read in both הוֺקִיעוּ √ יקע Lag We Dr and modern). 2 give a blast, blow (German 'stossen'), with ב of instrument (usually horn or clarion) Josh 6:4 , 8 , 9 , 13 (twice in verse); 6:16 , 20 (JE), Judg 3:27 ; 6:34 ; 7:18 (twice in verse); 7:19-20 , 14 t., + Num 10:3-4 , 8 , 10 (P; see חֲצֹצְרָה ), also Ezek 7:14 (see תָּקוֺעַ below); ׳ת alone Judg 7:20 ; Num 10:7 (P; opposed to חֵרִיעַ sound an alarm ), with accusative תְּרוּעָה 10:5 ; 10:6 ; 10:6 (P; see חֲצֹצְרָה ); with accusative of instrument Judg 7:22 ; Hosea 5:8 ; Isa 18:3 ; Jer 4:5 ; 6:1 ; 51:27 ; Joel 2:1 , 15 ; Psa 81:4 , + תקעו Josh 6:9 (Kt; Qr תֹּקְעֵי ). 3 strike, clap hands; in triumph, ׳ת עָלֶיךָ כַּף Nahum 3:19 , ׳ת כָ֑ף Psa 47:2 ; also (late) of gesture ratifying a bargain, specifically pledging oneself to become surety, only Proverbs (all || עַרַב ): ׳ת כַּמֶּיךָ לַזָּר Prov 17:18 ; 22:26 ; absolute 11:15 . Niph`al Imperfect 3masculine singular 1 שׁוֺפָר יִתָּקַע Amos 3:6 if a horn be blown , compare ׳יִתּ ׳בְּשׁ Isa 27:13 it shall be blown (a blast shall be given) on a horn. 2 ׃ יִתֵָּקעַ לְיָדִי מִיהֿוּא Job 17:3 who is there that will strike himself (i.e. pledge himself) into my hand ?","rootNote":"a primitive root;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 10 10","keyReferences"